  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/35546C">Definition <span data-tag="35546C">6.2.2.6</span>.</a>sheafShvC@$\Shv (\calC )$ Let $\calC $ be a $($small$)$ $\infty $-category equipped with a Grothendieck topology. Let $S$ be the collection of all monomorphisms $U \rightarrow j(C)$ which correspond to covering sieves $\calC ^{(0)}_{/C} \subseteq \calC _{/C}$. An object $\calF \in \calP (\calC )$ is a <em>sheaf</em> if it is $S$-local. We let $\Shv (\calC )$ denote the full subcategory of $\calP (\calC )$ spanned by $S$-local objects. </p>
